  "manual": [
    "Fleet: Smart Mode must be on for the fixture (the Trust dialog accepted, the backend downloaded) and the fixture built once (`cargo build` in it), so the debug run stops within the wait.",
    "Fleet keeps breakpoints with the workspace: regenerate the fixture (make-fixture.py) before a rerun, or the first click removes the breakpoint instead.",
    "macOS: macprobe.py sends the scene's chords through WEEP's keymap (`key` -> `mac`); F5, F9 and F10 go as they are. Attaching needs the debugger entitlement; the attach shots only open the dialog.",
    "2026-11-04 run: the disabled-breakpoint shots were dropped; Fleet's Go to Action knows no \"toggle enabled breakpoint\". Learn the title from `actions-breakpoint`, or the gesture from `breakpoint-menu`, and add the disabled shots back.",
    "2026-11-04 run: regenerate the fixture between the Fleet and the WEEP run (Fleet's console step typed into its editor and autosaved). Fleet opens the Debug tool in the right panel: its Variables 'Local' row is at about (938, 412) and 'Add Watch' at (1213, 380); focus the tool before Cmd+N (in the editor it makes a new file). Fleet debugs with Alt+Enter on the popup row.",
    "2026-11-05: coordinates after the stop taken from Fleet's batch 13 shots (both editors now put the Debug tool in the right panel): Step Into (822, 91), Variables' Local row (960, 412), Add Watch (1215, 380), the Debugger Console's input (420, 690), a click in the editor before Go to Line (640, 300). Both consoles are in 'commands' mode (WEEP's since d34d387): an expression needs a leading '?'.",
    "2026-11-05: Fleet showed nothing for quick evaluate (Cmd+Alt+E, its keymap's mac chord for debug/quick-evaluate-expression) at 5:23 within 2 s; try the editor's right-click menu or Go to Action next time."
  ],
